    "/internal/privacy/erase": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Erase a data subject. Called by compliance-service during a DSAR fan-out.\n\nReturns the ack: what was erased, and what was RETAINED with its legal basis. Idempotent \u2014 a\nDSAR retries, so erasing an already-erased subject must not fail. Wire this service into the\nfan-out by adding it to PRIVACY_TARGETS in compliance-service's values file; the\nsafety:privacy-wiring gate fails if you implement this and forget.",
        "operationId": "erase_subject_internal_privacy_erase_post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "header",
            "name": "X-Internal-Token",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "title": "X-Internal-Token"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EraseIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "additionalProperties": true,
                  "title": "Response Erase Subject Internal Privacy Erase Post",
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Erase Subject",
        "tags": [
          "internal"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/internal/verification/identity/{claim_ref}/seen": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Has this verified identity been seen before?\n\nThe anti-abuse question, asked by onboarding-service before it grants anything once per\nidentity. Internal tier because the caller is a SERVICE, not a person \u2014 a capability check\nwould have been machine auth wearing a user's clothes.\n\nTakes a claim_ref rather than a raw value on purpose: the caller must already hold the hash, so\nthis cannot be used to ask whether a given national id exists in our records. A raw-value\nendpoint here would be an enumeration oracle over a national registry.",
        "operationId": "identity_seen_internal_verification_identity__claim_ref__seen_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "claim_ref",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Claim Ref",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "header",
            "name": "X-Internal-Token",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "title": "X-Internal-Token"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "additionalProperties": true,
                  "title": "Response Identity Seen Internal Verification Identity  Claim Ref  Seen Get",
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Identity Seen",
        "tags": [
          "internal"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/internal/verification/sweep-pending": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Lapse verification prompts nobody answered. Called by the sweep CronJob.\n\nA safety net, not the authority: status() already refuses to trust a lapsed record, so a sweep\nthat has not run cannot leave one trusted. This keeps the store tidy and makes the lapse\nvisible, rather than leaving rows that look pending forever.",
        "operationId": "sweep_pending_internal_verification_sweep_pending_post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "header",
            "name": "X-Internal-Token",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "title": "X-Internal-Token"
            }
          }
